### Pruebas manuales de Products.Api desde Visual Studio
### (clic en "Enviar solicitud" sobre cada bloque, con la API corriendo)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5001

### Listar categorías (para el select del frontend)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/categories

### Crear producto → 201 Created
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mouse inalámbrico",
  "description": "Mouse óptico 1600 DPI",
  "categoryId": 1,
  "imageUrl": "https://example.com/mouse.png",
  "price": 15.50
}

### Crear producto inválido → 400 (nombre vacío y precio negativo)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "categoryId": 1,
  "price": -5
}

### Listado paginado con filtros dinámicos
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?name=mouse&categoryId=1&minPrice=10&page=1&pageSize=10

### Obtener por id → 200 o 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/1

### Editar → 200 (el stock no se puede cambiar aquí)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/products/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mouse inalámbrico Pro",
  "description": "Mouse óptico 3200 DPI",
  "categoryId": 1,
  "imageUrl": "https://example.com/mouse-pro.png",
  "price": 19.99
}

### Ajustar stock: compra de 20 unidades → 200
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/products/1/stock
Content-Type: application/json

{ "delta": 20 }

### Ajustar stock: venta mayor al stock → 409
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/products/1/stock
Content-Type: application/json

{ "delta": -999 }

### Eliminar (soft delete) → 204; luego GET del mismo id → 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/products/1
